IMPORT prelude

-- Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011 (Singapore) -- what a bank depositor or an insurance policy owner
-- gets if the bank or insurer fails: who is a DI Scheme member (s 5), what is an insured deposit (First Schedule), when compensation
-- may be paid (s 21), the depositor's entitlement and the $100,000 Maximum DI Coverage (ss 22, 23, 26), what is an insured policy
-- (s 2), the categories of insured policies and the protection ratios (s 47, Second and Fourth Schedules), refunds of premiums and
-- deductions (ss 47(6), 48, 48A(6), 48B), joint policies (s 49), settlement options (s 50A), and false statements about cover
-- (ss 67, 70, 71).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DIPOPSA2011.txt. The deposit
-- is headed "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 9/3/2025"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 5 of 2025 (wef
-- 9 March 2025, s 82). The Maximum DI Coverage of $100,000 is annotated S 706/2023 wef 1 April 2024.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: almost everyone in Singapore holds a bank account or an insurance policy,
-- and this Act says how much of it is protected if the bank or insurer fails. SCOPED to what a depositor or policy owner meets.
-- Not encoded: membership exemptions (ss 6, 7, 32, 33), the funds, premium contributions and levies (Parts 3, 4, 7, 8), prescribed
-- products and separate coverage under s 22(5), the Part 5A resolution withdrawals, subrogation and recovery (ss 27, 28, 52, 53),
-- transfer and run-off (s 54), liquidators (ss 28A, 29, 54A, 55), the Agency (Part 10), the Third Schedule formulas used for levies,
-- the general-business maximum compensation (s 48A(2), left to regulations not deposited), and offences other than ss 67, 70, 71.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011 -- compensation`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `5 -- DI Scheme members`

-- s 5(1): "Every full bank or finance company which is not exempted under section 6 is a DI Scheme member so long as it holds a
-- valid licence under the Banking Act 1970 or the Finance Companies Act 1967". A bank that is not a "full bank" is not named.
GIVEN `is a full bank or finance company` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exempted under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the institution is a DI Scheme member` IF
    `is a full bank or finance company` AND `holds a valid licence` AND (NOT `is exempted under s 6`)

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- insured deposits and insured depositors`

-- First Schedule: "insured deposit" means (a) deposits "in Singapore dollars, placed with any DI Scheme member in any of its branches
-- in Singapore" in (i) a savings account, (ii) a fixed deposit account, (iii) a current account, including credited interest,
-- "regardless of whether such a deposit is pledged, charged or secured as collateral"; (b) Singapore-dollar moneys placed under the
-- CPFIS, CPFRS or the Supplementary Retirement Scheme; (c) prescribed products; "but does not include any structured deposit".
-- s 2: "insured depositor" means any person "who is not an excluded person"; "excluded person" includes "(a) any bank".
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore dollar savings account`
    `a Singapore dollar fixed deposit`
    `a Singapore dollar current account`
    `Singapore dollar SRS moneys`
    `Singapore dollar CPF Investment Scheme moneys`
    `a foreign currency fixed deposit`
    `a structured deposit`
    `a unit trust bought through the bank`

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding is of an insured kind` IF
    CONSIDER `the holding`
    WHEN `a Singapore dollar savings account` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore dollar fixed deposit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Singapore dollar current account` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Singapore dollar SRS moneys` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Singapore dollar CPF Investment Scheme moneys` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Paragraph (a) requires a branch in Singapore. Paragraph (b) (CPFIS, CPFRS, SRS) does not say so; this encoding follows the words.
GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding, `with a DI Scheme member` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a branch in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the depositor is a bank` IS A BOOLEAN, `pledged as collateral` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the depositor holds an insured deposit` IF
        `the holding is of an insured kind` `the holding`
    AND `with a DI Scheme member`
    AND (NOT `the depositor is a bank`)
    AND (    `at a branch in Singapore`
         OR  `the holding` EQUALS `Singapore dollar SRS moneys`
         OR  `the holding` EQUALS `Singapore dollar CPF Investment Scheme moneys`)

§§ `21 -- when compensation may be paid`

-- s 21(1): where (a) a court orders a DI Scheme member wound up; (b) it is wound up voluntarily; or (c) "the Authority is of the
-- opinion that a DI Scheme member is insolvent, unable or likely to become unable to meet its obligations, or about to suspend
-- payments", "the Authority MAY determine that compensation be paid out of the DI Fund". No event pays out automatically.
GIVEN `a winding-up order is made` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is wound up voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN, `MAS thinks it insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `MAS may determine that compensation be paid` IF
    `a winding-up order is made` OR `it is wound up voluntarily` OR `MAS thinks it insolvent`

§§ `22, 23 and First Schedule -- how much a depositor gets`

-- First Schedule: "'Maximum DI Coverage' means the amount of $100,000." [S 706/2023 wef 01/04/2024]
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Maximum DI Coverage` MEANS 100000

-- s 23(3) (deposits) and s 49(2) (policies): joint holders are "deemed to have an equal share ... unless there is an express provision
-- to the contrary in the books" of the failed member.
GIVEN `the joint amount` IS A NUMBER, `number of holders` IS A NUMBER, `the books say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `share in the books` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the joint holder's share` MEANS
    IF `the books say otherwise` THEN `share in the books`
    ELSE `the joint amount` DIVIDED BY `number of holders`

-- s 22(1): deposits held (a) in the depositor's own right, (b) jointly, (c) in the name of the depositor's sole-proprietorship and
-- (d) SRS moneys are AGGREGATED, and compensation "must not exceed the aggregate amount of such insured deposits or the Maximum DI
-- Coverage, whichever is lower". s 22(6): "the liabilities (if any) that are owing from the insured depositor to the failed DI Scheme
-- member are disregarded" -- so `owed to the bank` is deliberately not used.
GIVEN `own-name deposits` IS A NUMBER, `share of joint deposits` IS A NUMBER, `sole-proprietorship deposits` IS A NUMBER,
      `SRS deposits` IS A NUMBER, `owed to the bank` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 22(1) compensation` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`own-name deposits` PLUS `share of joint deposits` PLUS `sole-proprietorship deposits` PLUS `SRS deposits`)
                   `the Maximum DI Coverage`

-- s 22(4): CPFIS and CPFRS moneys "must not be aggregated with the insured depositor's other insured deposits" and are compensated
-- up to the lower of the amount and the Maximum DI Coverage -- a SEPARATE cap.
GIVEN `CPF scheme deposits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 22(4) compensation` MEANS
    `the lower of` `CPF scheme deposits` `the Maximum DI Coverage`

-- s 22(2): deposits held "as trustee under a trust" or in "a client account" are compensated "in respect of every such account" up to
-- the lower of the amount in that account and the Maximum DI Coverage; (3) where two or more insured depositors hold that account
-- jointly, the compensation "must be divided equally among" them.
GIVEN `the trust account balance` IS A NUMBER, `number of trustees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each trustee's s 22(2) compensation` MEANS
    (`the lower of` `the trust account balance` `the Maximum DI Coverage`) DIVIDED BY `number of trustees`

§§ `26 -- mergers`

-- s 26(1): if two DI Scheme members merge (or one acquires the other's deposit-taking business) and the merged member fails "within
-- one year after the date of the merger", a depositor with deposits in both is compensated "as if the merger ... did not take place",
-- up to the Maximum DI Coverage for each original member. (2) The Minister may extend the period (not modelled).
GIVEN `deposits with the first bank` IS A NUMBER, `deposits with the second bank` IS A NUMBER,
      `failed within one year of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation after a merger` MEANS
    IF `failed within one year of the merger`
    THEN     `the lower of` `deposits with the first bank` `the Maximum DI Coverage`
        PLUS `the lower of` `deposits with the second bank` `the Maximum DI Coverage`
    ELSE `the lower of` (`deposits with the first bank` PLUS `deposits with the second bank`) `the Maximum DI Coverage`

§§ `2 -- insured policies`

-- s 2: "insured policy" means (a) any life policy; (b) any accident and health policy; (c) any compulsory insurance policy (motor
-- third-party risks; work injury compensation); or (d) "any specified personal line insurance policy which is a Singapore policy".
-- "specified personal line insurance policy" means a policy "issued to a natural person" providing (a) personal motor cover;
-- (b) personal travel cover; (c) personal property (structure and contents) cover; (d) cover in connection with the employment of a
-- foreign domestic worker.
DECLARE Policy IS ONE OF
    `a life policy`
    `an accident and health policy`
    `a motor third-party policy`
    `a work injury compensation policy`
    `a personal motor policy`
    `a personal travel policy`
    `a home contents policy`
    `a foreign domestic worker policy`
    `a commercial property policy`

GIVEN `the policy` IS A Policy, `issued to a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Singapore policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy is an insured policy` IF
    CONSIDER `the policy`
    WHEN `a life policy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an accident and health policy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a motor third-party policy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a work injury compensation policy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commercial property policy` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `issued to a natural person` AND `a Singapore policy`

§§ `47 and Second and Fourth Schedules -- life policies`

-- Second Schedule (simplified to whole policies): Category 1 -- individual accident and health policies, group health and group
-- personal accident policies; Category 2 -- any other individual policy, and voluntary group term, whole life and endowment policies;
-- Category 3 -- individual annuities and voluntary group annuities; Category 4 -- non-voluntary group term, whole life, endowment and
-- annuity policies. (Riders and benefit-by-benefit classification are not modelled.)
DECLARE LifeCover IS ONE OF
    `an individual hospitalisation policy`
    `a group health policy`
    `an individual whole life policy`
    `an individual endowment policy`
    `a voluntary group term policy`
    `an individual annuity`
    `a non-voluntary group term policy`

GIVEN `the cover` IS A LifeCover
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Second Schedule category` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cover`
    WHEN `an individual hospitalisation policy` THEN 1
    WHEN `a group health policy` THEN 1
    WHEN `an individual whole life policy` THEN 2
    WHEN `an individual endowment policy` THEN 2
    WHEN `a voluntary group term policy` THEN 2
    WHEN `an individual annuity` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 4

-- Fourth Schedule para 1: Maximum Sum Assured $500,000; Maximum Surrender Value $100,000; Maximum Annuity Sum $100,000; Maximum Group
-- Sum Assured $100,000; Maximum Group Surrender Value $50,000. Para 2: each protection ratio is "the ratio of the Maximum ... to the
-- aggregate amount" guaranteed on the life assured "or 1, whichever is lower". Category 1: the ratio is 1.
GIVEN `the maximum` IS A NUMBER, `the aggregate on the life` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the protection ratio` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate on the life` AT MOST `the maximum` THEN 1
    ELSE `the maximum` DIVIDED BY `the aggregate on the life`

-- s 47(2)(a): Category 1 -- the protection ratio (1) times "the amount of policy moneys payable".
GIVEN `policy moneys payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Category 1 compensation` MEANS
    `policy moneys payable` TIMES 1

-- s 47(2)(b)(i) with Fourth Schedule para 2(b): Category 2 sum assured -- the ratio of $500,000 to the aggregate sum assured on the
-- life assured under all such policies, times the sum assured under this policy.
GIVEN `sum assured under this policy` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate sum assured on the life` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Category 2 sum assured compensation` MEANS
    (`the protection ratio` 500000 `aggregate sum assured on the life`) TIMES `sum assured under this policy`

-- s 47(2)(b)(ii) with para 2(c): Category 2 surrender value (where written notice to surrender was given before the quantification
-- date) -- the ratio of $100,000 to the aggregate guaranteed surrender value, times this policy's guaranteed surrender value.
GIVEN `surrender value of this policy` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate surrender value on the life` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Category 2 surrender value compensation` MEANS
    (`the protection ratio` 100000 `aggregate surrender value on the life`) TIMES `surrender value of this policy`

-- s 47(2)(c) with para 2(d): Category 3 -- the ratio of $100,000 to the aggregate commuted value of guaranteed annuity benefits, times
-- "the amount of policy moneys guaranteed to be payable under the annuity". So an annuity is scaled down, not capped at a sum.
GIVEN `guaranteed annuity payment` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate commuted value on the life` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Category 3 annuity compensation` MEANS
    (`the protection ratio` 100000 `aggregate commuted value on the life`) TIMES `guaranteed annuity payment`

-- s 47(2)(d)(i) with para 2(e)(i): Category 4 -- "in respect of each life assured per policy", the ratio of the Maximum Group Sum
-- Assured ($100,000) to the sum assured under EACH group policy. Not aggregated across policies.
GIVEN `group sum assured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Category 4 sum assured compensation` MEANS
    (`the protection ratio` 100000 `group sum assured`) TIMES `group sum assured`

-- s 47(6): where a claim event has occurred, or the policy has been terminated, on or before the quantification date, "there must be
-- deducted ... (a) any outstanding loan taken out against that insured policy; and (b) any outstanding premiums". Contrast s 22(6),
-- under which a depositor's debts to the bank are disregarded. (Whether the result can go below nil is not said; not modelled.)
GIVEN `gross compensation` IS A NUMBER, `outstanding policy loan` IS A NUMBER, `outstanding premiums` IS A NUMBER,
      `claim event or termination before the quantification date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the life compensation after s 47(6) deductions` MEANS
    IF `claim event or termination before the quantification date`
    THEN `gross compensation` MINUS `outstanding policy loan` MINUS `outstanding premiums`
    ELSE `gross compensation`

§§ `48, 48A(6), 48B -- refunds of premiums and general policies`

-- s 48(1) (life) and s 48B (general): where the policy owner "is expressly entitled under the contract of insurance" to a refund of
-- premiums, a covered party is entitled to compensation "for the premiums in full".
GIVEN `premiums refundable under the contract` IS A NUMBER, `expressly entitled to a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the premium refund compensation` MEANS
    IF `expressly entitled to a refund` THEN `premiums refundable under the contract` ELSE 0

-- s 48A(1): general policies -- "the aggregate amount of the protected liabilities", (2) "subject to the maximum amount of compensation
-- that is prescribed by the Authority" (regulations not deposited, so the cap is a parameter here); (6) where a claim event has occurred
-- or the policy terminated on or before the quantification date, "reduced by the amount of all outstanding premiums". No loan deduction.
GIVEN `protected liabilities` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER, `outstanding general premiums` IS A NUMBER,
      `claimed or terminated before the quantification date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general policy compensation` MEANS
    IF `claimed or terminated before the quantification date`
    THEN (`the lower of` `protected liabilities` `the prescribed maximum`) MINUS `outstanding general premiums`
    ELSE `the lower of` `protected liabilities` `the prescribed maximum`

§§ `50A -- settlement options`

-- s 50A(2): where "a settlement option ... has been exercised before the quantification date", the policy "ceases to be covered under
-- the PPF Life Fund" and no compensation is due. (3) A settlement option is an option on surrender, maturity or claim to leave the
-- moneys with the insurer to accrue interest or be invested, or to take instalments. (4) It applies only if no further policy moneys
-- are payable on any contingency after the option is exercised.
GIVEN `a settlement option was exercised before the quantification date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no further policy moneys are payable after it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the policy remains covered by the PPF Life Fund` IF
    NOT (`a settlement option was exercised before the quantification date` AND `no further policy moneys are payable after it`)

§§ `67, 70, 71 -- false statements about cover`

-- s 67(1): "No person may, knowingly or recklessly, make a false or misleading statement as to whether or not" (a) a person is a DI
-- Scheme member, (b) a PPF Scheme member, (c) a deposit or product is an insured deposit, or (d) a policy is an insured policy.
-- (2) an offence "even though a contract does not come into being": a fine up to $125,000 or 3 years or both, and up to $12,500 a day
-- for a continuing offence. s 71(1): for a corporation, a fine "not exceeding 2 times the maximum amount". s 70: the general penalty
-- where none is provided is $50,000.
GIVEN `made a statement about cover` IS A BOOLEAN, `the statement was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is an offence under s 67` IF
    `made a statement about cover` AND `the statement was false or misleading` AND `knew or was reckless`

GIVEN `is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 67 fine` MEANS
    IF `is a corporation` THEN 2 TIMES 125000 ELSE 125000

-- In months.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 67 imprisonment` MEANS 36

GIVEN `is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum general-penalty fine` MEANS
    IF `is a corporation` THEN 2 TIMES 50000 ELSE 50000
